From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:44:19 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Leave every network and Google service permission out of
 TalkBack

TalkBack in this build holds no network access and no Google service
permission. The manifests request none of INTERNET, ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE,
READ_GSERVICES and the AICore BIND_SERVICE (the Google Analytics, Primes
and Gemini permissions), nor the unused GET_PACKAGE_SIZE; the braille
display library's INTERNET request goes as well. The platform adds
ACCESS_LOCAL_NETWORK only to an application that holds INTERNET, so the
application holds none of the three. The braille keyboard's request for
the receiver guard permission of Google's own package goes too: nothing
declares it, and its receiver is registered not exported.

Everything that needed those permissions is absent from the interface
instead of disabled:

- The Gemini configuration reports the image description, the image
  question and the screen overview as off, so the "Detailed image
  descriptions" switch and the entries that depend on it are not shown.
  The voice command setting stays hidden.
- The dynamic features (icon and image descriptions that download
  libraries) are reported as unsupported, which removes the Automatic
  descriptions screen, the "Describe image" context menu rule, gesture
  action and menu setting, and the image caption storage.
- NetworkUtils reports no connection, and PackageManagerUtils reports no
  Google Play services, whatever the platform holds.
- The settings entries that open a web page or a store page are hidden:
  privacy policy, terms of service, Play Store, Google support, the
  survey and help and feedback.
- The "Learn more" button of the punctuation dialog and the help center
  button of the new key map dialog, which started a browser the image
  does not carry, are removed. So is the support page link of the braille
  keyboard's change gesture dialog: the dialog drops the last paragraph of
  its message, which every translation sets apart by a blank line.
- The three tutorial links to the image description pages and the
  keyboard tutorial's image description section are removed, so that no
  tutorial page names a feature this build lacks and no link is dead.
- The voice typing shortcut needs Gboard, which the image does not
  carry, so its flag is off: no dialog asks to update Gboard, the New
  features pages and the gesture list do not offer it, the gesture
  practice page names the two-finger double tap "play or pause media",
  and the double tap stays play/pause.
- A stored "Summarize view" or "Describe image" gesture or key combo is
  unassigned while the capability is off: the shared command entry
  returns no feedback, so no stored value opens the online opt-in dialog.
- Google Assistant is not offered: the two tutorial tips that recommend
  it and the voice command help entry are removed, and the "assistant"
  voice command no longer starts an activity.
- The keymap changes page shows no Google help link, and the new key map
  dialog no longer carries the help center address. Its text still says
  "help center" in every language, because it has no separate sentence.

The Gemini code stays compiled but unreachable: every entry point checks
the flags above, and no request can leave the application without the
permission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
